From 8f98b9de4bc5770ba0a4ceb1725408fe2e9d16f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:07:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 76/78] test: check OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S against the M4 vectors
 of p2mr-ts

p2mr-ts, the TypeScript P2MR library, was written independently, with
its own BIP 341 and SLH-DSA code (@noble/post-quantum). Its vectors for
these rules, vectors/m4/p2mr_m4_spend.json and p2mr_m4_construction.json
from its support for them, which is not published yet, are copied
unmodified into src/test/data/; p2mr_ts_m4_vectors.md has their SHA-256.
p2mr_ts_m4_tests recomputes every value of theirs this code base can
compute:

- each of the 11 spends: the tapleaf hash, the control byte, the spent
  scriptPubKey from the control block, the signature messages for
  key_version 0, 1 and 2 (33 in all) and the file's own preimage of the
  message; the witness element sizes and layout; the 10 signatures,
  verified with SLHDSA128SVerify or MLDSA44Verify; and the whole witness
  through VerifyScript with the flags of these rules. The six spends through leaf
  versions 0xc0 and 0xe0 pass, and fail with SLHDSA128S_SIG once a bit of
  the signature is flipped; the unsigned one fails with EVAL_FALSE. The
  four through leaf version 0xe2 (pq2) use a leaf version this series
  does not implement: there they succeed without executing, as an
  unknown leaf version does, and policy refuses them;
- the construction: the three SLH-DSA public keys from their seeds, the
  nine SLH1 leaves in three leaf versions, and six trees with their leaf
  hashes, Merkle roots, scriptPubKeys, control blocks and signet and
  regtest addresses; for pq2 also the S1 leaf from the ML-DSA-44 key and
  that key's SHA-256.

Every value agreed. The copies are replaced only on purpose, together
with their hashes.
